                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17725b77-4998-3c76-a0a4-308dabc08c70",
                                        "entry_id": "5764e4e1-8027-3b65-ba05-e33561fb5d89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act or state of being sentimental."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "435e4ab9-157f-4093-a4fc-b84149583209",
                                                "sense_id": "17725b77-4998-3c76-a0a4-308dabc08c70",
                                                "text": "Things that were implicit and largely unjudged in the book, filtered through layers of stiff-upper-lip irony — Fanny’s self-pity, Linda’s obliviousness — are now foregrounded and, for the most part, rendered banal, with “Beaches”-level platitudes and sentimentality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f5b5473-f4b1-4d28-9218-39b697052203",
                        "source_entry_id": "2f61ded1-c11e-39fe-ba65-0f609df2e768",
                        "source_sense_id": "4bd52eab-d8f3-3b80-b7da-b771c0fb5e5a",
                        "source_sense_description": "ohne Plural, oft abwertend: zu große Empfindsamkeit",
                        "target_lang_word": "sentimentalité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sentimentalité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "227e828f-20d9-3745-a768-03dd926f85d0",
                                        "entry_id": "c185ea35-e82a-3416-98f2-7380f7de655f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Affectation de sentiment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16ef4b96-5035-453d-889d-df0f71260f12",
                                                "sense_id": "227e828f-20d9-3745-a768-03dd926f85d0",
                                                "text": "Donc, plus de fausse pudeur ni de sensiblerie de mauvais aloi. Plus de sentimentalités stériles, dommageables, le plus souvent exagérées, et dont ne sont même plus dupes les passants — aux coups de chapeaux convenus devant les corbillards."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23c9deb9-b1e0-4aee-a646-6f4419941ca2",
                                                "sense_id": "227e828f-20d9-3745-a768-03dd926f85d0",
                                                "text": "Peut-être l’affectation est-elle comme la sentimentalité, dont Alain-Fournier a dit en substance que c’en est quand ce n’est pas réussi et que c’est de l’art, du drame et de la vie quand ça l’est."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
